out god "\n\rMusic: 'In the locust wind comes a rattle and hum'\n\rThe juke bops: 'See them burning crosses, see the flames, higher and higher'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Jacob wrestled the angel and the angel was overcome'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Bullet the blue sky'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Plant a demon seed, you raise a flower of fire'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Bullet the blue'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'See them burning crosses, see the flames, higher and higher'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Suit and tie comes up to me'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Bullet the blue sky'\n\rThe juke bops: 'His face red'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Bullet the blue'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Like a rose on a thorn bush'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Suit and tie comes up to me'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Like all the colours of a royal flush'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'His face red'\n\rThe juke bops: 'And he's peeling off those dollar bills'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Like a rose on a thorn bush'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Slapping them down, one hundred, two hundred,'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Like all the colours of a royal flush'\n\rThe juke bops: 'And I can see the fighter planes'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'And he's peeling off those dollar bills'\n\rThe juke bops: 'And I can see the fighter planes'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Slapping them down, one hundred, two hundred,'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Across the mud huts as the children sleep'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'And I can see the fighter planes'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Through the alleys of a quit city street'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'And I can see the fighter planes'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Up the staircase to the first floor'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Across the mud huts as the children sleep'\n\rThe juke bops: 'We turn the key and slowly unlock the door'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Through the alleys of a quit city street'\n\rThe juke bops: 'A man breathes deep into a saxophone'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Up the staircase to the first floor'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Through the walls we hear the city groan'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'We turn the key and slowly unlock the door'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Outside is America'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'A man breathes deep into a saxophone'\n\rThe juke bops: 'Outside is America'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Through the walls we hear the city groan'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Outside is America'\n\rThe juke starts playing Frank Zappa, Camarillo Brillo.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Outside is America'\n\rThe juke bops: 'She had that Camarillo brillo'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rThe juke bops: 'Flamin' out along her head,'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: Frank Zappa, Camarillo Brillo\n\rThe juke bops: 'I mean her Mendocino bean-o'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'She had that Camarillo brillo'\n\rThe juke bops: 'By where some bugs had made it red'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'Flamin' out along her head,'\n\rThe juke bops: 'She ruled the Toads of the Short Forest'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'I mean her Mendocino bean-o'\n\rThe juke bops: 'And every newt in Idaho'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'By where some bugs had made it red'\n\rThe juke bops: 'And every cricket who had chorused'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'She ruled the Toads of the Short Forest'\n\rThe juke bops: 'By the bush in Buffalo'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9\n\rMusic: 'And every newt in Idaho'\n\rThe juke bops: 'She said she was a Magic Mama'\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
